hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1090","Chapter on whose guarantee of safety is valid, and on returning detachments to the main army, 1128 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Mecca in the year of the Conquest, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us as a preacher and said: O people, whatever alliance there was in the pre-Islamic age, Islam has only strengthened it; there is no alliance in Islam. The Muslims are one hand against others besides them; the lowest of them grants protection on their behalf, the furthest of them returns spoils to them, their detachments return to those who stayed behind, a believer is not killed for a disbeliever, the blood-money of a disbeliever is half the blood-money of a believer, there is no bringing animals to be milked at the collector nor taking them away from him, and their charities are taken only in their own dwellings."
